Hi,

please allow me to "fire" back with another basic question. For a good glm, the residuals should be approximately normally distributed. Again, with corpus data, how strictly do I have to apply this requirement? Is it reasonable to decide based on a normality test or is there more room for "approximation"?

Thanks and regards,
Anne

