> For a good glm, the residuals should be approximately normally distributed.

That is not quite accurate, plus there are many kinds of residuals of
glms. Fox & Weisberg is one of the best sources on all this that I
know, they have a whole chapter on this kind of stuff and a variety of
functions to explore regression diagnostics.

> Again, with corpus data, how strictly do I have to apply this requirement?

Hm, why should there be a special degree of strictness for corpus
data? I would think all the normal rules apply.

STG
