Not a naive question at all but also one that is not easy to answer without writing a chapter ;-) Fox & Weisberg's main point seems to be that one wants to see a constant conditional mean function of the residuals across the range of (a) predictor(s), which seems to be the pretty similar to constant variance of residuals in an lm. However, the same logic as before applies:you also want to make sure that whether apparent violations of normality you find are due to influential data points so I would still recommend looking for those (the car package has many functions that help with that) and throwing in some bootstrapping for good measure.

